<title>USA: Weitzer says settles lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Weitzer says settles lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI LAKES, Fla. 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Weitzer Homebuilders Inc said Thursday that a lawsuit against the company concerning the convertibility of debentures into common stock has been settled.</p>
<p>The lawsuit had been filed by UC Financial Ltd and Universal Finance Holding AG concerning the convertibilty of an aggregate $600,000 principal amount of debentures into common stock.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the settlement, the debentures were redeemed by the company for $690,000, including accrued interest. In addition, the company redeemed a debenture in the principal amount of $300,000 for $320,000, which includes accrued interest.</p>
<p>The company said no shares of Class A common stock were issued as a result of the redemptions.</p>
<p>Weitzer Homebuilders designs, builds and sells single-family homes.</p>
</text>
